    <!-- The physical rows, by brand and then model: no emulator machine;
         the image base is the board's flash. The four RP2350 rows (the
         Pimoroni Pico Plus 2 and Pico Plus 2 W, the Raspberry Pi Pico 2
         and Pico 2 W: the same chip, the same 520K window, the same
         collector row) share one core object, one system-call object
         and one heap and collect object, frozen under the Pico 2's row
         and named for the chip, beside the an505 row's other Cortex-M33
         objects; the U5A5's row links its own heap object (the least
         managed heap the row guarantees differs from the an505 row's)
         and shares every other object with the an505 row, the core
         included; the STM32F769 row links its own core, system-call, heap
         and collect objects (the board's row fields differ from the
         emulator row's). -->
